{
  "id": "COMPOUND:31453 - PROTEIN:3941",
  "verbalization": "Cis-Bis(Methylthio)Silvatin is implicated in the target relationship with Alpha-actinin-1 through a chain of molecular interactions. The drug is directly linked to Phosphatidylinositol transfer protein alpha isoform, which in turn is a target of Galbanic Acid and 8-O-(P-Coumaroyl)-1(10)E,4(5)E-Humuladien-8-Ol, all of which ultimately target Alpha-actinin-1. This suggests that Cis-Bis(Methylthio)Silvatin may exert its effects by modulating the activity of these proteins, potentially through a mechanism involving phosphatidylinositol transfer or lipid metabolism. The evidence supports a pathway where the drug influences a series of proteins involved in lipid transport and signaling, with Alpha-actinin-1 being a downstream target. The integration of these targets highlights a possible role for Cis-Bis(Methylthio)Silvatin in regulating cellular processes through indirect interactions with lipid-related pathways.",
